ing someone else that  he has to explain it to or somebody  who's got to put it into perspective  just it's just him and her and they got  to work  so if there's a weak point to this  episode it's that the actual plot is  kind of bog-standard not just for Doctor  Who but for sci-fi shows in general for  decades I mean it's a very old trope guy  who's after something and says it's for  this thing that seems fairly innocuous  but turns out it's for a bad thing I  mean this this is beyond a standard plot  the episode I think more or less gets  away with it though because ultimately  the plot is not the point we're here for  a character study we are here for Maisie  Williams character and to spend time  with her and to get to know her and we  do get that we get that very well  executed it's just that even taking into  consideration it still feels like it's  just too generic for its own good when I  think of other episodes that focused  heavily on the supporting character  things like Vincent and the doctor or  the girl in the fireplace those both had  stronger stories in addition to really  solid character study work that said all  there are some good elements I really  did like Sam Swift that specially you  know standing up there just trying to  run out the clock and get the crowd on  his side that would that was just  wonderful and fun and it wasn't  gratuitous either it served a purpose  too especially when the doctor points  out you know we need the mayflies we  need the people who embrace every moment  that they have because they know it's  precious and I really did like that  conversation between him and her in that  tavern afterwards because I wasn't quite  in my mind coming up with whoa why won't  he take her with him but I think the way  that he explained it just worked really  well I like the name drop for Captain  Jack Harkness I wish I could say that I  think that's kinda lead to something I I  don't really I think it was just well  you know that's obviously the other  immortal character that we've got in the  show yeah sure let's name-dropping but  it's not it's nice to think about the  two of them running into each other that  would be very cool I do hope we see  Maisie Williams character again and I  think that hint that we caught at the  very end with the her showing up in the  selfie is an indicator that maybe we're  not done with her and we'll get more out  of her it's one of those things where I  wish secretly sheshe could become  something like River Song where she  would just get dropped in every now and  then and doesn't get overused but  unfortunately the problem is because she  is still young she's not gonna you know  retain that same look she's they have  every year going forward she's gonna be  a little bit older she's gonna look a  little bit older and since they've  established eight hundred years she  didn't physically age that doesn't work  so whatever they're gonna do with her  they kind of have to do this series  maybe out of stretch they couldn't drop  her into series 10 but I think beyond  that they're not gonna be able to keep  using her I think the note that things  ended between them was really  interesting I'm intrigued to see what  it'll be like the next time they meet  each other that's now six episodes into  the series not a bad step yet so I guess  we'll leave it at that did you catch  this episode if you did what were your  thoughts on it whatever they were drop  something down in the comments and let's  talk about it until next time this  council is adjourned  [Applause]
 

